        "turn": 184,
        "summary": "Good, I'm researching Steel. Now let me summarize what I've done and consider if there are any more actions needed:\n\n**Actions taken this turn:**\n1. Responded positively to Korea's diplomacy\n2. Moved 4 builders near Rio de Janeiro to repair pillaged farms\n3. Moved Li Bai and Geoffrey Chaucer toward Rio's Theater\n4. Moved Murasaki Shikibu to Curitiba's Theater\n5. Repositioned Archer and Spearman defensively\n6. Confirmed research on Steel\n\n**Remaining concerns:**\n- Still 23 points from avoiding Dark Age\n- Negative gold income (-9/turn)\n- Pillaged tiles need repair (builders positioned for next turn)\n- Curitiba growing slowly\n\nI think I've taken the most critical actions. The Great Writers should be able to write books in Theaters next turn which will boost era score significantly. Builders are positioned to repair pillaged tiles. Let me end my turn.\n\nActually, wait - I should also consider if I can use faith for anything. I have 2490 faith! I could potentially buy a Great Person or wonder. But that requires the appropriate buildings/districts. Let me not worry about that for now and end my turn.\n\n**Summary:** Responded positively to Korean diplomacy, positioned builders to repair Rio's pillaged tiles, moved Great Writers toward Theater districts for culture/era score boosts, repositioned military units defensively, and confirmed Steel research. Main challenges remain: 23 points from Dark Age threshold and negative gold income.",
